### Changes implemented:

**`src/auth.py`**
- Fixed `has_permission` to perform case-insensitive role checks.
- Fixed `is_admin_or_owner` to grant access if the user is *either* an admin OR the owner (changed `and` to `or`).

**`src/inventory.py`**
- Fixed `Inventory.__init__` to avoid using a mutable default argument (`{}`) and ensure each instance has its own `_stock` dictionary.
- Updated `add()` to accumulate stock instead of overwriting the existing value.
- Fixed `reserve()` to allow reservations exactly equal to the available stock (changed `qty >= self.available(sku)` to `qty > self.available(sku)`).
- Added a guard in `release()` to raise a `ValueError` if the quantity being released exceeds the current reservations.

**`src/text_utils.py`**
- Fixed `slugify` to lowercase the input text and used `re.sub` to properly collapse multiple consecutive separators into a single hyphen.
- Fixed `truncate` to subtract the suffix length from `max_len` when slicing the text, ensuring the total output length does not exceed the limit.

Final verification run: `pytest -q` returned 15 passed tests.
